# What clang-format formats, and which clang-format - THE ONLY PLACE THIS LIVES.
#
# Everything that formats this repository reads this file, so it is edited here
# and nowhere else:
#
#   .github/workflows/clang-format-check.yml   through scripts/clang-format-exclude.sh
#   .githooks/pre-commit                       through scripts/clang-format-exclude.sh
#   Extras/clang-format-all-win64/*.bat        directly, where the repository has one
#
# Before this file existed the list was written out once per reader, and the
# copies had drifted. Add a vendor directory here and nowhere else.
#
# FORMAT
#   clang-format-version: <x.y.z>
#                        the clang-format CI runs, named as DoozyX names its
#                        builds. The pre-commit hook formats with exactly this
#                        version or not at all, so the two never undo each
#                        other's work. Exactly one line.
#   source-root: <dir>   a directory clang-format runs over, relative to the
#                        repository root; empty = the whole repository. Opens a
#                        section. Repeat it for another root; no root may
#                        contain another.
#   <path>               a path relative to the source root above it, no
#                        trailing slash. Excludes that exact file, or that
#                        directory and all of it.
#   # ...                a comment, on its own line. Blank lines ignored.
#
# Vendor code, generated code and data tables only. If you are excluding
# something we wrote, fix the formatting instead.

